# CODEX CLI (OPENAI) — COMPREHENSIVE ARCHITECTURAL ANALYSIS

## 1. PROJECT IDENTITY & PURPOSE

**Codex CLI** is OpenAI's locally-run coding agent. It is:
- A command-line agent that executes coding tasks autonomously on your machine
- Available as standalone binary (macOS, Linux, Windows), npm package (`@openai/codex`), or Homebrew
- Integrated into ChatGPT Pro/Business/Edu plans; can also use API keys
- Part of a larger ecosystem: Codex Web (cloud-based), Codex IDE integrations (VS Code, Cursor, Windsurf)
- **Problem domain**: Autonomous code generation, modification, testing, and project understanding

**Entry points**:
- CLI: `codex` (TUI mode) → [codex-rs/cli/src/main.rs](codex-rs/cli/src/main.rs)
- Subcommands: `codex app` (desktop), `codex mcp` (MCP server), `codex login`, `codex doctor`
- App Server (daemon): JSON-RPC protocol over IPC → [codex-rs/app-server/src/lib.rs](codex-rs/app-server/src/lib.rs)

