## 6. LLM PROVIDER ABSTRACTION

### Multi-Provider Support

**Trait**: [model-provider/src/provider.rs](codex-rs/model-provider/src/provider.rs) `ModelProvider`

```rust
pub trait ModelProvider: Debug + Send + Sync {
    fn info(&self) -> &ModelProviderInfo;
    fn capabilities(&self) -> ProviderCapabilities { ... }
    fn approval_review_model(&self) -> &str { ... }
    fn memory_extraction_model(&self) -> &str { ... }
    // ...
}
```

**Implementations**:
1. **OpenAI** (default): Chat Completions & Responses API
   - Provider ID: `chatgpt` (via auth)
   - Endpoint: `https://api.openai.com/v1/responses`
2. **Amazon Bedrock**: Runtime provider
   - Provider ID: `amazon-bedrock`, `amazon-bedrock-runtime`
   - Region-based auth (SigV4)
3. **Local models**: `lmstudio`, `ollama` (config-driven)
4. **API key auth**: Fallback support

**Responses API**: Proxied via [responses-api-proxy](codex-rs/responses-api-proxy/)
- Listens on ephemeral port
- Forwards POST `/v1/responses` to OpenAI
- Dumps request/response for debugging

### Streaming & Model Features

- **Streaming**: SSE (Server-Sent Events) parsing in [realtime_conversation.rs](codex-rs/core/src/realtime_conversation/)
- **Prompt caching**: Supported via Responses API headers
- **Reasoning models** (o3/o4): Parameter `reasoning_effort` in config; handled transparently
- **Vision**: Image encoding via `image-rs` + URL passing
- **Function calling**: Native tool_choice + function_call in Responses API

### Failure Recovery

**Provider auth recovery**: `ProviderUnauthorizedRecovery::Recovered` trigger re-auth flow

