## 13. SANDBOXING / SAFETY

### Sandbox Abstraction

**Trait**: [core/src/tools/sandboxing.rs](codex-rs/core/src/tools/sandboxing.rs)

```rust
pub trait Sandboxable {
    fn sandbox(&self) -> SandboxType;
    fn permissions(&self) -> SandboxPermissions;
}

pub struct SandboxAttempt {
    pub sandbox: SandboxType,           // None, LinuxLandlock, Linux, Windows, Seatbelt
    pub permissions: SandboxPermissions,
    pub exec_server_permissions: ExecServerPermissions,
    pub enforce_managed_network: bool,
    // ...
}
```

### Platform-Specific Implementations

**macOS** ([core/src/sandboxing/](codex-rs/core/src/sandboxing/)):
- Seatbelt (`/usr/bin/sandbox-exec`) + profile
- File read/write whitelisting
- Network restrictions

**Linux** ([linux-sandbox/src/lib.rs](codex-rs/linux-sandbox/src/lib.rs)):
- **Landlock** (if kernel ≥ 6.2): Filesystem ACLs in process
- **Bubblewrap** (bwrap): Container-like filesystem isolation
- **seccomp**: System call filtering
- **no_new_privs**: Prevent privilege escalation

**Windows** ([windows_sandbox.rs](codex-rs/core/src/windows_sandbox.rs) + [windows-sandbox-rs/](codex-rs/windows-sandbox-rs/)):
- **RestrictedToken** (default): Limited privileges
- **Elevated** (opt-in): Admin privileges for build tools
- Filesystem restrictions via handle restrictions
- Registry read-only

### Permission Model

**SandboxPermissions**:
```rust
pub struct SandboxPermissions {
    pub read_paths: Vec<FileSystemPath>,
    pub write_paths: Vec<FileSystemPath>,
    pub execute: bool,
    pub network: NetworkPolicy,
}
```

**Defaults**:
- Read: CWD + project roots (auto-detected)
- Write: CWD
- Execute: Enabled (unless escalated)
- Network: Blocked by default (managed network proxy when needed)

### Network Approval

**Deferred**: [tools/network_approval.rs](codex-rs/core/src/tools/network_approval.rs)

```
Tool requests network access
    ↓
DeferredNetworkApproval spawned
    ├─ User notified
    ├─ Tool execution paused
    └─ Awaits network approval
    
Approval granted
    ├─ Managed network proxy enabled
    └─ Tool resumes with network access
```

